  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the strongest result so far (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), while image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is weak (0.208 accuracy). It is unclear whether the multiprofile avgpool benefit seen in RNA also applies to the image branch, which is critical before investing in multimodal fusion. config_011 tests this cleanly by keeping ResNet50 and changing only the profile/aggregation setting to multiprofile avgpool relative to config_010. This is the best next experiment because it isolates an important design choice, reduces uncertainty about whether image features can contribute, and avoids prematurely adding fusion or changing multiple factors."
